From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:55:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(desktop): finished chats paint green without
 being opened

Problem: in an example Desktop sidebar most finished chats show no green stripe and turn
green only once navigated to (Admin's screenshots, example incident).

Why 1: an idle stored-done row paints `done` only if
useWorkSourceUnavailable() is false; for every unopened row it was true.
  evidence: session-dot-state.ts sessionStatusStripe gate (sourceUnavailable
  && !userBlocked ...), session-row-stripe.tsx calls the hook per row.
Why 2: the hook required a positive, current-epoch read of all five work
sources (lineage, tasks, process, subagent, control) for EVERY row.
  evidence: use-work-source-unavailable.ts -> !workSourceAuthorityComplete().
Why 3: process / subagent / control are read only for the displayed chat
(session-control.ts refreshSessionControl for the open runtime), so no other
row can ever collect them: unread == unavailable kept them grey until opened,
when the reads ran and green appeared.
Root (happened): PR #1697 (ddb2e8b16e11, "unavailable authoritative work
source holds done") made "never read" mean "unavailable" for all rows, a
fail-closed rule designed around the focused chat and applied to rows that
are structurally never read.
Root (not caught): its tests certified rows by hand-feeding all five reads
(certifyRow in session-row.test.tsx, capture()/succeed() elsewhere), and the
one unread-row test asserted the grey stripe as intended behaviour; no test
modelled an unfocused row as the app actually leaves it (no reads).
Recurrence: first time for this cause.

Fix:
- The displayed chat (main pane or a tile: runtime role a/t, new
  workSourceSessionDisplayed) keeps the strict rule: every source must be
  positively read for its current authority; a rebind still revokes proof.
- Any other row is vetoed only by evidence: a pending or failed read of its
  CURRENT authority epoch, or a route with no live authority (socket closed /
  not tracked) (new workSourceVetoed). A source never read for it, or a read
  from an obsolete epoch, is no evidence: its stored outcome decides, as
  before #1697. An unknown owner still vetoes.

Tests (RED on main, GREEN here):
- session-row: stored-done row with no reads paints `done`; a pending current
  read holds it `waiting`.
- session-tab-accent: unread authority no longer vetoes a stored-done tab.
- session-control-authority-routing: undisplayed unread row keeps `done`, a
  pending current read greys it; the strict primary-replacement / mirror-
  rebind / unread-before-first-poll cases now run on the displayed chat.
- work-source-secondary-authority: after a real reconnect an old failed reply
  cannot veto, a fresh failed read does; closed socket still vetoes.
Proof: vitest src/store src/lib src/app/chat 737 files / 7711 tests pass;
tsc --noEmit clean for apps/desktop/src.
